<p>In Mombasa you can also wander through the old town, with its narrow streets and old buildings, or sit with a coffee or juice and watch the street life. A ride on the ferry across the channel can be a fun shared experience, and a meal of seafood, samosas or coastal snacks in a busy place is a good way to talk. Check opening times and any entry fees yourself beforehand, and avoid quiet, isolated beaches for a first meeting.</p>

