<h2>Markets, cafes and street food</h2>
<p>Almost every Kenyan town has a market, and markets are good for dates. You get lots to look at, things to talk about and plenty of people around. Try fruit you have never tasted, share roasted maize or a snack, and chat with the stall owners. It is relaxed, affordable and full of personality.</p>
<p>A simple cafe is another reliable option. Pick a busy, welcoming place with good light and music that is not too loud. Order something small, and enjoy the conversation. If you prefer something more active, try a short walk around a town centre, a public garden or a museum. If you want a heartier meal, nyama choma in a busy, well-known spot is a very Kenyan way to share an hour or two.</p>

<h2>Plan the details, not just the place</h2>
